[{:seon.task/name "vectors-clean-is-a-commit"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `seon.vector/round` keeps :clean, the db at which everything due was asked, so the next round embeds only `seon.vector/written` between it and main (a datoms-diff); under churn it pins a stale version, and the :embedded ask carries a db too. Correct: :clean and the :embedded ask keep {:t :commit}, and round makes the base with d/commit-as-db before `written` (the diff reads the same nodes). Replaces the db values in the proc's state with references (AGENTS section 4). Cost: one more call per round; `seon.vector-cost-test/a-commit-is-embedded-for-what-it-changed` moves by the measured delta."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.writer/main-notices-carry-a-commit-not-a-db"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.vector-cost-test/a-commit-is-embedded-for-what-it-changed seon.vector-test/a-caught-up-round-diffs-from-its-clean-commit}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-model-is-loaded-outside-root"
  :seon.task/plan "Built (branch jolt/the-model-runs-in-its-own-process, for the owner's review): the model runs in `target/seon embed-worker` (seon.vector/serve!), an exec'd helper, because a fork cannot load it (docs/failure-points.md#physics-who-may-run-threads). The :embed kind's worker holds a handle with no process (seon.vector/open); seon.vector/embed starts the helper with the first batch and speaks seon.sock's frames over its pipes; the owner (seon.fx/owner-proc, a kind declaring :close) tells the worker {:idle true} when its queue is empty and nothing is in flight, and seon.vector/close ends the helper by closing its stdin; a death is :seon.vector/helper-died to the batch and the next batch starts another. A request that says :more (main's backlog) keeps the helper up for its next round. Replaces the in-root load and :seon.config.vector/model-threads (root has no model threads). Measured 2026-10-29: root 1,675 MB with the model, 1,128-1,149 MB with the helper (gone once the queue emptied); backlog 5,593 texts about 70 s with and without the helper (with :more; 210 s without it); a search on an idle root 1.24 s at load 14, 7 ms warm. Docs: docs/vector.md#the-model, docs/failure-points.md. Left to the owner: whether :more stays (a helper kept up on a :more that never comes holds 350-550 MB until the next request)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.vector-test/root-holds-no-model-after-an-embed}}]
